# DESK30, a FOLDER shortcut (`#V`): drag the SUB folder out of the C:\ window
# onto the desktop surface, then double-click the icon it makes. A folder
# shortcut opens a window on its own path (`do_open`'s `AT_ISFOLD` arm,
# `desksupp.c:1231-1259`), it does not launch anything.
#
#   B_WIN1      the C:\ window open
#   C_SHORTCUT  the SUB shortcut on the desktop
#   D_OPENED    the window it opened, titled C:\SUB\
#
# Coordinates from d-probe: 'SUB' in window 1 box (477,87) -> click (515,103);
# the free bottom-row cell the d30 run used is box (182,433) -> click (220,449).
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1500 move 37 42
1700 down
1703 up
1710 down
1713 up
2300 move 600 240
3000 mark B_WIN1
3400 move 515 103
3700 down
3800 drag 250 458
4400 up
4600 move 600 300
5200 mark C_SHORTCUT
5600 move 220 449
5800 down
5803 up
5810 down
5813 up
6400 move 600 300
7200 mark D_OPENED
